---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title="Kavach \u00b7 Pricing and free pilot" description="Try Kavach on your own data, free for 90 days, installed inside your environment." current="pilot/" height={4000}>
<!-- HERO + FORM -->
<section style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px 104px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 56px; align-items: flex-start">
<div style="flex: 1 1 460px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Free pilot · 90 days</p>
<h1 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-weight: 650; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: clamp(42px, 5.4vw, 72px); line-height: 0.98; letter-spacing: -0.02em; text-wrap: balance">Try Kavach on your own data.</h1>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--kv-ink-2); text-wrap: pretty">We install Kavach in your environment and help you compare it with what you use today. None of your records are sent to us.</p>
<ol style="list-style: none; margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; border-top: 1px solid var(--kv-ink)">
<li style="display: flex; gap: 20px; padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--kv-line)"><span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: var(--kv-indigo); padding-top: 3px">01</span><span style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px"><strong style="font-size: 18px">Install inside your network</strong><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Containers on your own servers, with sizing worked out together.</span></span></li>
<li style="display: flex; gap: 20px; padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--kv-line)"><span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: var(--kv-indigo); padding-top: 3px">02</span><span style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px"><strong style="font-size: 18px">Run it on your real agent traffic, calls or documents</strong><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Your data stays where it is. Only you see the results.</span></span></li>
<li style="display: flex; gap: 20px; padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--kv-line)"><span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', monospace; font-size: 14px; color: var(--kv-indigo); padding-top: 3px">03</span><span style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px"><strong style="font-size: 18px">Compare with what you use today</strong><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Use the public evaluation harness to score both on the same data.</span></span></li>
</ol>
</div>

<div style="flex: 1 1 440px; min-width: 0; background: var(--kv-paper); border: 1px solid var(--kv-line); border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -36px rgba(22, 26, 46, 0.35); padding: 30px">
<form id="pilot-form" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-weight: 650; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: 30px">Book a pilot</h2>
<label class="kv-field">Name<input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label>
<label class="kv-field">Work email<input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required></label>
<label class="kv-field">Company<input type="text" name="company" autocomplete="organization" required></label>
<fieldset style="border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<legend style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; padding: 0 0 8px">What do you need to redact?</legend>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px">
<button type="button" class="kv-choice" data-need="AI agent and LLM traffic" aria-pressed="true">AI agent and LLM traffic</button>
<button type="button" class="kv-choice" data-need="Calls and recordings" aria-pressed="false">Calls and recordings</button>
<button type="button" class="kv-choice" data-need="Documents and images" aria-pressed="false">Documents and images</button>
<button type="button" class="kv-choice" data-need="Text, logs and databases" aria-pressed="false">Text, logs and databases</button>
</div>
</fieldset>
<button class="kv-btn" type="submit" style="font: inherit; font-weight: 600; font-size: 17px; background: var(--kv-indigo); color: var(--kv-paper); border: 0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 16px; cursor: pointer">Book a pilot</button>
<p id="pilot-error" role="alert" style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--kv-vermilion-deep)" hidden>Something went wrong sending your request. Please email us instead.</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--kv-muted)">We only use these details to set up the pilot.</p>
</form>
<div id="pilot-done" role="status" style="flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; min-height: 360px; justify-content: center" hidden>
<svg aria-hidden="true" width="44" height="48" viewBox="0 0 26 28" fill="none"><path d="M13 1.5l11 4v8c0 6.2-4.6 11.2-11 13-6.4-1.8-11-6.8-11-13v-8z" stroke="#1E2C6B" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M8 14l3.5 3.5L18.5 10" stroke="#1E2C6B" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
<h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-weight: 650; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: 30px">Request received.</h2>
<p id="pilot-done-text" style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">We’ll write to the email you gave to plan the install.</p>
<button id="pilot-reset" class="kv-btn2" type="button" style="align-self: flex-start; font: inherit; font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; background: transparent; color: var(--kv-ink); border: 1px solid var(--kv-ink); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 18px; cursor: pointer">Edit request</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- PRICING -->
<section id="pricing" style="background: rgba(239, 235, 224, 0.72); border-top: 1px solid var(--kv-line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--kv-line)">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 104px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px">
<div class="rv" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; max-width: 720px">
<h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-weight: 650; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.04">Pricing</h2>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">An annual licence with no per-call or per-page fees, so you can redact everything, not just a sample.</p>
</div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 16px">
<article class="rv" style="background: var(--kv-paper); border: 1px solid var(--kv-line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 30px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px">Single product</h3>
<div style="font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1">[PRICE] <span style="font-family: 'Mukta', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--kv-muted)">/ year</span></div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">One of Relay, Voice or Vision, plus Core, on one production cluster, with email support.</p>
</article>
<article class="rv" style="background: var(--kv-indigo-deep); color: var(--kv-on-dark); border: 1px solid var(--kv-indigo-deep); border-radius: 8px; padding: 30px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px"><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px">Platform</h3><span style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid var(--kv-on-dark-muted); color: var(--kv-on-dark); padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 3px">Most teams</span></div>
<div style="font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1">[PRICE] <span style="font-family: 'Mukta', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--kv-on-dark-muted)">/ year</span></div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-on-dark-2)">Every product, unlimited volume, GPU builds, real-time voice, priority support and a model update every quarter.</p>
</article>
<article class="rv" style="background: var(--kv-paper); border: 1px solid var(--kv-line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 30px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px">OEM and custom</h3>
<div style="font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1">Talk to us</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Embed Kavach in your own product, or have us tune it to your documents, languages and ID formats.</p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 104px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column">
<h2 class="rv" style="margin: 0 0 24px; font-family: 'Anek Latin Variable', sans-serif; font-weight: 650; font-stretch: 85%; font-size: clamp(30px, 3.6vw, 42px); line-height: 1.06">Before you start</h2>
<details style="border-top: 1px solid var(--kv-ink); padding: 20px 0"><summary style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600">What hardware does it need?<span class="kv-plus" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--kv-indigo); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1">+</span></summary><p style="margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Core and Relay run on CPUs. For real-time Voice and high-volume Vision, a single GPU is enough. We work out sizing with you during the pilot.</p></details>
<details style="border-top: 1px solid var(--kv-line); padding: 20px 0"><summary style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600">Can we add our own ID formats?<span class="kv-plus" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--kv-indigo); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1">+</span></summary><p style="margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">Yes. You can add validators for policy, claim and account numbers in minutes. New entity types or languages are a custom tuning engagement.</p></details>
<details style="border-top: 1px solid var(--kv-line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--kv-line); padding: 20px 0"><summary style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600">Does any of our data reach you during the pilot?<span class="kv-plus" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--kv-indigo); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1">+</span></summary><p style="margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--kv-ink-2)">No. The pilot runs on your infrastructure, the same way production does. <a href={u('dpdp/')}>More on security</a>.</p></details>
</section>
</Base>

<script>
import { initPilotForm } from '../lib/pilot';
initPilotForm();
</script>
